    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0580" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/11045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-17T19:00:00+01:00">June 17, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 17—3:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2185. Department’s 1206, June 16, 3 p.m. Swedish Government has informed Germans
                    that all transit shipments of goods to either Norway or Finland via Bothnian
                    route must cease by August 1.</p>
                <p>My 590, June 17, 7 p.m. repeats this to London with reference to my 462, May 24,
                        midnight.<anchor n="84" xml:id="d534-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
